specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:19:- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:20:- Registering a static tool with an invalid schema type throws an error naming that tool ([validated by: names the tool when registration rejects an invalid static schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L5)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:22:- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules ([validated by: validates each dynamic schema and reuses a schema object validator](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L21)).
